Title: Khaman Dhokla Recipe (Fluffy & Soft)

Channel: indianhealthyrecipes.com

Linked recipe blog structured data (schema.org Recipe JSON-LD) — prefer this for method text when it has instructions:

{
  "@type": "Recipe",
  "name": "Khaman Dhokla Recipe (Fluffy & Soft)",
  "author": {
    "@id": "https://www.indianhealthyrecipes.com/#/schema/person/2d7d264cdc5dc6602ee06a087cd3fcb0"
  },
  "description": "I&#39;ll help you make the BEST instant Dhokla at home under 30 mins. Gram flour, salt, a leavening agent and tempering spices come together to make this savory steamed cake. It&#39;s soft, fluffy and moist that you no more want to order or eat it out.",
  "datePublished": "2020-11-09T11:06:07+00:00",
  "image": [
    "https://www.indianhealthyrecipes.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/11/khaman-dhokla-recipe.jpg",
    "https://www.indianhealthyrecipes.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/11/khaman-dhokla-recipe-500x500.jpg",
    "https://www.indianhealthyrecipes.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/11/khaman-dhokla-recipe-500x375.jpg",
    "https://www.indianhealthyrecipes.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/11/khaman-dhokla-recipe-480x270.jpg"
  ],
  "video": {
    "name": "Khaman Dhokla",
    "description": "Find the written recipe here on our website -",
    "uploadDate": "2026-08-04T13:52:04+00:00",
    "duration": "PT30S",
    "thumbnailUrl": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi/LvUJ5iDzT80/hqdefault.jpg",
    "embedUrl": "https://www.youtube.com/embed/LvUJ5iDzT80?feature=oembed",
    "contentUrl": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LvUJ5iDzT80",
    "@type": "VideoObject"
  },
  "recipeYield": [
    "4",
    "4 to 5"
  ],
  "prepTime": "PT10M",
  "cookTime": "PT20M",
  "totalTime": "PT30M",
  "recipeIngredient": [
    "1 + ¼ cup (300 ml) water",
    "1 teaspoon (5 grams) natural citric acid ((or 2 tablespoon lemon juice or use yogurt, read notes))",
    "3 tablespoon sugar",
    "1 to 1¼ teaspoon sea salt",
    "2 tablespoons (30 ml) oil ((peanut or coconut oil))",
    "1 tablespoon ginger (fine grated or ¾ tbsp paste)",
    "2 green chilies ((deseed and mince or paste, omit for kids))",
    "2 tablespoons (20 grams) fine semolina ((fine suji/ rava, to omit cut down 3 tbsps water))",
    "2 cups (220 grams) besan ( (gram flour))",
    "¼ teaspoon turmeric",
    "1½ teaspoon (8 grams) Eno ( (unflavored fruit salt or 1 teaspoon baking soda))",
    "1 tablespoon oil ((15 ml))",
    "1 teaspoon mustard seeds",
    "2 slit green chilies ( (adjust to preference))",
    "12 curry leaves",
    "1 teaspoon white sesame seeds ( (optional))",
    "¼ teaspoon hing ( (asafoetida, optional))",
    "1 tablespoon sugar ((adjust to taste))",
    "½ teaspoon sea salt ( (adjust to taste))",
    "1 to 1½ cup water ((240 to 360 ml))",
    "1 to 2 tablespoons raw grated coconut (or desiccated)",
    "1 to 2 tablespoons coriander leaves ( fine chopped)"
  ],
  "recipeInstructions": [
    {
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "text": "Grease a 7 to 8 inch round or square cake pan or a steel container. Line a parchment if using an aluminum or non-stick coated pan.",
      "name": "Grease a 7 to 8 inch round or square cake pan or a steel container. Line a parchment if using an aluminum or non-stick coated pan.",
      "url": "https://www.indianhealthyrecipes.com/khaman-dhokla/#wprm-recipe-69856-step-0-0"
    },
    {
      "@type": "HowToSection",
      "name": "How to make Khaman Dhokla",
      "itemListElement": [
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "text": "In a large mixing bowl, whisk together water, citric acid, sugar, salt, oil, ginger paste, chili paste and semolina, until the sugar dissolves.",
          "name": "In a large mixing bowl, whisk together water, citric acid, sugar, salt, oil, ginger paste, chili paste and semolina, until the sugar dissolves.",
          "url": "https://www.indianhealthyrecipes.com/khaman-dhokla/#wprm-recipe-69856-step-1-0"
        },
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "text": "Place a sieve and add the besan and turmeric. Sieve and mix well to a lump free smooth batter.",
          "name": "Place a sieve and add the besan and turmeric. Sieve and mix well to a lump free smooth batter.",
          "url": "https://www.indianhealthyrecipes.com/khaman-dhokla/#wprm-recipe-69856-step-1-1"
        },
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "text": "Whisk very well in one direction for 40 to 60 seconds. Cover and rest for 10 mins.",
          "name": "Whisk very well in one direction for 40 to 60 seconds. Cover and rest for 10 mins.",
          "url": "https://www.indianhealthyrecipes.com/khaman-dhokla/#wprm-recipe-69856-step-1-2"
        },
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "text": "Pour 3 cups water to a steamer and place a high-legged trivet or a rack. Bring it to a boil.",
          "name": "Pour 3 cups water to a steamer and place a high-legged trivet or a rack. Bring it to a boil.",
          "url": "https://www.indianhealthyrecipes.com/khaman-dhokla/#wprm-recipe-69856-step-1-3"
        },
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "text": "When the water begins to boil, add eno and a tablespoon of water. Mix until well combined, thick and frothy, taking care not to overdo.",
          "name": "When the water begins to boil, add eno and a tablespoon of water. Mix until well combined, thick and frothy, taking care not to overdo.",
          "url": "https://www.indianhealthyrecipes.com/khaman-dhokla/#wprm-recipe-69856-step-1-4"
        },
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "text": "Transfer to the greased pan and steam on a medium to medium high heat for 18 mins, until a tester comes out clean. (8 inch pan – 18 mins, 7 inch pan – 20 mins)",
          "name": "Transfer to the greased pan and steam on a medium to medium high heat for 18 mins, until a tester comes out clean. (8 inch pan – 18 mins, 7 inch pan – 20 mins)",
          "url": "https://www.indianhealthyrecipes.com/khaman-dhokla/#wprm-recipe-69856-step-1-5"
        },
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "text": "Cool down completely on a wire rack.",
          "name": "Cool down completely on a wire rack.",
          "url": "https://www.indianhealthyrecipes.com/khaman-dhokla/#wprm-recipe-69856-step-1-6"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@type": "HowToSection",
      "name": "Make the Tempering",
      "itemListElement": [
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "text": "Heat oil on a medium flame and add mustard seeds. When they begin to splutter, add curry leaves & green chilies.",
          "name": "Heat oil on a medium flame and add mustard seeds. When they begin to splutter, add curry leaves & green chilies.",
          "url": "https://www.indianhealthyrecipes.com/khaman-dhokla/#wprm-recipe-69856-step-2-0"
        },
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "text": "When the leaves turn crisp, add sesame seeds and fry for a minute. Add hing, sugar, salt as needed and pour water.",
          "name": "When the leaves turn crisp, add sesame seeds and fry for a minute. Add hing, sugar, salt as needed and pour water.",
          "url": "https://www.indianhealthyrecipes.com/khaman-dhokla/#wprm-recipe-69856-step-2-1"
        },
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "text": "Bring to a rolling boil and mix until the sugar dissolves. Turn off and cool down to warm.",
          "name": "Bring to a rolling boil and mix until the sugar dissolves. Turn off and cool down to warm.",
          "url": "https://www.indianhealthyrecipes.com/khaman-dhokla/#wprm-recipe-69856-step-2-2"
        },
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "text": "When the khaman dhokla cools down, invert it on a tray and slice it to 16 squares. (If you did not use a parchment, run a knife around the sides to loosen it from the pan)",
          "name": "When the khaman dhokla cools down, invert it on a tray and slice it to 16 squares. (If you did not use a parchment, run a knife around the sides to loosen it from the pan)",
          "url": "https://www.indianhealthyrecipes.com/khaman-dhokla/#wprm-recipe-69856-step-2-3"
        },
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "text": "Spoon the floating spices on to the khaman and pour the water all over, (optionally reserve ¼ cup to pour while serving). Garnish with coconut and chopped coriander leaves, both optional.",
          "name": "Spoon the floating spices on to the khaman and pour the water all over, (optionally reserve ¼ cup to pour while serving). Garnish with coconut and chopped coriander leaves, both optional.",
          "url": "https://www.indianhealthyrecipes.com/khaman-dhokla/#wprm-recipe-69856-step-2-4"
        },
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "text": "Serve khaman dhokla with coriander/ cilantro chutney and red chutney.",
          "name": "Serve khaman dhokla with coriander/ cilantro chutney and red chutney.",
          "url": "https://www.indianhealthyrecipes.com/khaman-dhokla/#wprm-recipe-69856-step-2-5"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
