  "review": [
    {
      "@type": "Review",
      "reviewRating": {
        "@type": "Rating",
        "ratingValue": "5"
      },
      "reviewBody": "My first time making khaman dhokla and it tasted very good. I used lemon juice and baking soda because that's what I had. Next time will try with eno and citric acid to see if there is any difference. Thank you",
      "author": {
        "@type": "Person",
        "name": "Darshana"
      },
      "datePublished": "2026-09-11"
    },
    {
      "@type": "Review",
      "reviewRating": {
        "@type": "Rating",
        "ratingValue": "5"
      },
      "reviewBody": "I made and it turned out delicious. I took it my work place to share with my friends. They loved it with the hari chutney. Anyone taking it to a potluck, carry the tempered water in a thermos and pour it while slightly hot. It instantly softened and made the dhokla perfect.",
      "author": {
        "@type": "Person",
        "name": "Tara"
      },
      "datePublished": "2026-08-25"
    },
    {
      "@type": "Review",
      "reviewRating": {
        "@type": "Rating",
        "ratingValue": "5"
      },
      "reviewBody": "Beautiful dhokla recipe. Turned out as shown",
      "author": {
        "@type": "Person",
        "name": "Sameera"
      },
      "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
    },
    {
      "@type": "Review",
      "reviewRating": {
        "@type": "Rating",
        "ratingValue": "5"
      },
      "reviewBody": "I always struggled to find the right pan for my dhokla. This recipe gave me the idea to use my masala dabba because I didn't have any steel containers. My dhokls turned out very spongy and tasted yummy. Since my bowl was big, not 5 inch I steamed only for 12 mins. My sis-n-law always adds fresh lemon juice in the tadka. I did the same and it was the best I ever made.",
      "author": {
        "@type": "Person",
        "name": "Divya"
      },
      "datePublished": "2026-06-25"
    },
    {
      "@type": "Review",
      "reviewRating": {
        "@type": "Rating",
        "ratingValue": "5"
      },
      "reviewBody": "Love your recipes very much and this dhokla is our favorite. I follow the recipe to the T but make the tadka in ghee. Excellent flavor!",
      "author": {
        "@type": "Person",
        "name": "Farah"
      },
      "datePublished": "2026-06-22"
    },
    {
      "@type": "Review",
      "reviewRating": {
        "@type": "Rating",
        "ratingValue": "5"
      },
      "reviewBody": "Should i cool the tempering water before pouring over the cut dhoklas ?",
      "author": {
        "@type": "Person",
        "name": "Katkar"
      },
      "datePublished": "2026-04-23"
    },
    {
      "@type": "Review",
      "reviewRating": {
        "@type": "Rating",
        "ratingValue": "5"
      },
      "reviewBody": "It turned out perfect. 👌👌",
      "author": {
        "@type": "Person",
        "name": "Vandana Nair"
      },
      "datePublished": "2026-03-14"
    }
  ],
